Lobium — native audio-fingerprint farbling of the upstream sample TAPS (AudioWorklet + ScriptProcessorNode).

Closes the two deterministic-offline bypasses documented as follow-ups after the main audio farbling
(fingerprint/audio-context.patch): a page can read the rendered/processed audio samples UPSTREAM of the
farbled OfflineAudioContext result buffer via (a) AudioWorkletProcessor.process(inputs) or (b) the
deprecated ScriptProcessorNode.onaudioprocess event.inputBuffer. Both are deterministic inside an
OfflineAudioContext, so an adversary could read un-farbled audio through them. This patch farbles those
JS-visible input surfaces with the same kernel + keying as the result buffer.

Both taps are GATED TO OFFLINE contexts only — realtime AudioWorklet/ScriptProcessorNode do genuine DSP
on audio that is played, and are timing-jittery (not a stable fingerprint), so perturbing them would be
both a violation of the "never touch played audio" principle and pointless. Offline detection:
  - Worklet: AudioWorkletGlobalScope::IsOfflineContext() — a default-false flag that ONLY
    OfflineAudioWorkletThread sets at global-scope creation (realtime/semi-realtime threads leave it
    false). Read from the processor via its global_scope_.
  - ScriptProcessorNode: !context()->HasRealtimeConstraint() (OfflineAudioContext returns false).

Both farble the JS-VISIBLE copy, never the shared graph signal:
  - Worklet: input_array_buffers_ (the V8 arrays handed to process() as `inputs`) is farbled AFTER
    CopyPortToArrayBuffers copies the AudioBus INTO it — the source AudioBus the graph reuses downstream
    is untouched.
  - SPN: external_input_buffer_ (the AudioProcessingEvent.inputBuffer) is a readback artifact — playback
    flows through external_output_buffer_, so real audio output is unaffected.

LobiumFpConfig::Current() is safe to call from the worklet render thread: it is a base::NoDestructor
static (thread-safe init guard), immutable after init, with thread-safe init inputs (CommandLine
singleton + pure base64), and it is initialized early on the main thread before any worklet runs.

Keyed identically to the OfflineAudioContext result hook (one key per (seed, absolute frame) across all
channels of a quantum): base_index = the worklet render frame (currentFrame) / the SPN playback frame
(playback_time*sampleRate), seed = cfg->seeds.audio. seed 0 (or realtime) => passthrough.

Proven on Chromium 152.0.7928.0 (SwiftShader): offline worklet input-sum and offline SPN input-sum are
both host-differing, stable-per-seed, and distinct-per-seed (~0.001% imperceptible shift). No regression:
the main offline result farble is unchanged (gcd=235885ed), user-created AudioBuffers stay bit-exact
under a seed (playback safety), and the detector gate holds at 9/9 surfaces / sannysoft 0-fail.

Four hook points touch existing files (this patch); no added files, no BUILD.gn change (all in the wired
blink modules component), no config change (seeds.audio already parsed):
  1. modules/webaudio/audio_worklet_global_scope.h — the is_offline_context_ flag + getter/setter.
  2. modules/webaudio/offline_audio_worklet_thread.cc — sets the flag at offline global-scope creation.
  3. modules/webaudio/audio_worklet_processor.cc — farbles the offline worklet's JS inputs.
  4. modules/webaudio/script_processor_node.cc — farbles the offline SPN's inputBuffer.
